{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/587200-vigor-and-improvised-weapon","id":587200,"title":"Vigor and Improvised Weapon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-11T09:49:52-07:00","id":587200,"title":"Vigor and Improvised Weapon","content":"Improvised Weapons Rules (p. 179):<br /> The weapons charts can only go so far. Characters who grab improvised weapons still stand a chance of doing serious damage.<br /> If your improvised weapon is close enough to one of the weapons above, use the associated weapon profile. Otherwise, an improvised weapon does (Durability \u2013 1) damage, with an initiative penalty and Strength requirement equal to the weapon\u2019s Size.<br /> Using an improvised weapon reduces your attack pool by one die. On a successful attack, the weapon takes the same amount of damage as it inflicts; Durability reduces this damage as normal. Once the weapon\u2019s Structure is reduced to 0, the object is wrecked.<br /> <br /> Vigor rules (p. 142):<br /> Lift and hurl objects normally far too unwieldy to use as weapons, such as boulders, cars, and other people. Any object she can lift, with Size no greater than her Strength, can be used as an improvised melee or throwing weapon. Improvised weapons have a weapon bonus equal to the lower of their Size or Durability. Objects with Size greater than 5 deal lethal damage to mortals, while those with Size 10 or more deal lethal even to vampires.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t understand how to put it all together.<br /> <br /> 1. Object\u2019s Size IS already the Strength requirement to use it as a weapon. Vigor passively increases Strength. The use of Vigor here seems senseless.<br /> <br /> 2. Damage rating is different. The standart rules state that Damage is Durability-1. Vigor rules state it the lower of Durability and Size. The question arises, what if the object is Size 1 and Durability 3?<br /> <br /> 3. The improvised weapons rules say, the weapon takes damage equal to the one dealt with it. Vigor rules say that it gets Damage in case the other active power is turned on \u2013 which adds to the Damage.<br /> <br /> 4. The usual combat rules say that any weapon deals lrthal damage to mortals. Vigor rules say that only objects with Size 5+ deal lethal.<br /> <br /> 5. Improvised Weapon rules mention initiative penalty. Vigor rules don\u2019t.<br /> <br /> So, it seems to me that that Vigor rules were written without considering Improvised weapon rules and should be fixed. Shouldn\u2019t they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 07-11-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T11:08:41-07:00","id":587254,"title":"","content":"1- This use isn't because of Size. It is to use UNWIELDY weapons. Your ST can, without this, reason that a car, a person or a boulder is to much unwieldy to begin with. If you can't hold the object properly, so no amount of strength will do it. Now you can pass this reasoning altogether.<br /> <br /> 2-5- Maybe you're right, and I agree that this use of Vigor needs revision, but also have in mind that this use is PRECISELY to change Improvised Weapons Rules. It just makes sense that the goal should be to make huge Improvised Weapons do moar damage, easier and without so much penalties.<br /> <br /> Probably it should be:<br /> <br /> 2- Change the calculation so greater size means greater damage even with less Durability. Maybe it could change to Durability +1, but no greater than Size. To be just Size would make it far to good.<br /> <br /> 3- To be precisely that means that Vigor would somewhat protect the weapon from such kind of recoil damage. Well, since the first sentence already implies an alteration in your relationship with the object's properties, and you did spent blood to inflict a more impressive side of your curse upon the world, I think it is just right. As long as you don't overtax your weapon even more, Vigor protects it from the result of being used as a weapon.<br /> <br /> 4- Probably should be fixed. Maybe it could be changed for reduced Defense from targets, since the weapon is too huge to dodge.<br /> <br /> 5- Not saying it should be that way, but if you are using a point of Vitae already to wield such a big thing as a weapon, it makes sense that you aren't hindered in your Initiative by said weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T11:41:37-07:00","id":587281,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\">monteparnas</a>, </b>well, I'm think about these changes:<br /> 1) Yep, I got your idea. Seems right.<br /> 2) Yepp.<br /> 3) Not agree. Just let the another active power of Vigor add Vigor to damage that any (including non-improvised) weapon takes from the strike. Durability still applies. It will smash improvised weapons and even hurt proper weapons too.<br /> 4) Any weapon does lethal to mortals and bashing to vampires. Size 5+ does lethal to vampires. Size 10+ does aggravited to mortals. Size 15+ (yep, Blood Potency 10) does aggravated to vampires.<br /> 5) Yepp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T12:12:50-07:00","id":587329,"title":"","content":"Still think 3 could work. Using Vigor to improve damage (effectively making Vigor be applied two times, once to hit, with already damages, another directly to damage) seems a lot of stress upon the weapon to bypass said protection.<br /> <br /> And, in game terms, such protection would mean turn a big improvised weapon a bit more reliable. As long as you just use this power of Vigor, you don't have to think of yet ANOTHER huge boulder or thing to use as weapon.<br /> <br /> I do prefer to avoid Aggravated Dmg, so maybe 10+ could be reducing Defense: it does start to get too big (and, by what we see in not having any Initiative penalty, still fast enough) to properly avoid. It could be -2 to Defense for each Size above 9 (you're being hit with a wall). But I can see a Size 5 object causing enough area damage to a vamp body to be Lethal for the Undead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby